# Player game manual

Authoritative player handbook lives under **`docs/manual/`**. GDD/TDD/UI/AI SPECs remain the sole sources of truth for behavior; the manual must never contradict them. On conflict, fix the manual.

Normative writing conventions: [`docs/manual/STYLE_GUIDE.md`](../../docs/manual/STYLE_GUIDE.md). ToC: [`docs/manual/index.md`](../../docs/manual/index.md). Updater workflow: `.cursor/skills/update-game-manual/SKILL.md`.

## When this rule applies

- Editing any file under `docs/manual/**`.
- Editing `SPEC/game/**`, `SPEC/ui/**`, or an allowlisted `SPEC/program/` file (below).

## Required-review trigger

A PR **must** review affected manual chapters (update them, or explicitly justify no update) when it modifies:

- any path under `SPEC/game/**`
- any path under `SPEC/ui/**`
- any of these allowlisted files:
  - `SPEC/program/orders.md`
  - `SPEC/program/turn-resolution-phases.md`
  - `SPEC/program/turn-resolution-phase-details.md`
  - `SPEC/program/order-engine.md`

**Advisory only** (no mandatory review): every other `SPEC/program/**` path. Authors may still update the manual if the change affects what the player can do, see, or be told.

Do **not** reintroduce a subjective “behavior-relevant” qualifier — use this allowlist only.

Identify affected chapters by **exact string match** of changed SPEC paths against each chapter’s `## Sources` bullets (see style guide).

## Manual update principles

1. **Player angle** — Explain why the player uses the mechanic and how it affects winning or enjoyment; do not merely restate a rule diff.
2. **Tone** — Vizier advising a young monarch; modern clear body prose; archaic flourishes only in Counsel callouts.
3. **Chapter template** — Purpose; How it is done; Counsel; The other courts; Consequences; Acceptance criteria for this chapter; Sources (last `##`).
4. **Sources footer** — Last `##` is exactly `## Sources`; each bullet is one backtick-wrapped repo-relative SPEC path with no trailing prose.
5. **Draft surfaces** — Omit, or cite as `**[DRAFT]** \`SCREENID\``; never operable steps in How it is done.
6. **Screen IDs** — Cite UI by stable 8-char IDs from `SPEC/ui/screen-registry.md`.
7. **Honesty** — Document only implemented, specced behavior; no exploit min-max guides.

## PR checklist (manual-impacting)

- [ ] Required-review paths listed above were checked against chapter `## Sources` footers.
- [ ] Affected chapters updated **or** PR body justifies non-update.
- [ ] Player-angle framing preserved; tone contract respected.
- [ ] Draft citations use `**[DRAFT]** \`SCREENID\`` or are omitted.
